  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{7}(-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
